ua->playback.channels = fmt_playback->bNrChannels;
ua->capture.frame_bytes = fmt_capture->bSubframeSize * ua->capture.channels;
Reason:
The driver retrieves channel counts from the USB descriptor without validating they are non-zero. If bNrChannels is zero, frame_bytes becomes zero, which is later used as a divisor in playback_urb_complete() and capture_urb_complete(), causing a division by zero kernel crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!ua->capture.channels || !ua->playback.channels) {
    dev_err(&ua->dev->dev,
            "invalid channel count: capture %u, playback %u\n",
            ua->capture.channels, ua->playback.channels);
    return -EINVAL;
}
Reason:
This sanity check ensures that the channel counts are non-zero before they are used to compute frame_bytes. If either is zero, the function returns an error, preventing the division by zero in the URB completion handlers.

